# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-18). L §3.6: "Shares that are holes leave one hole part of the remainder, 1 less the
# known shares, whose possible owners are the parties whose shares are holes (§8.1). A known share is never lost to a
# hole." L §8.1: "A read of q is a hole only for a q it may be" (HOLE-PART, `<place>: <amount> may be <q>'s:
# <questions>`); "The place's total stays known throughout". ania's share is half, tomek's a hole: ania 50.00, a hole
# part of 50.00 that may be tomek's, the couple's 0 (scratch/exp4.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
input half: num
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then half else 0
  rule unknown beats base = ?"what share is tomek's" when p == tomek
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania_tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  half = 0.5
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, ?"konto: 50.00 PLN may be tomek's: what share is tomek's" (konto), 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
